        "content": "<p>I'm trying to add optional docstring support to custom command syntax that involves <code>declare_syntax_cat</code>, but adding <code>(docComment)?</code> before the custom syntax category causes parsing failures. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#project=lean-nightly&amp;\">MWE (tested on Lean nightly):</a></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Command</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">declare_syntax_cat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myKeyword</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myKeyword</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test1</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Works: without docComment</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myCmd1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myKeyword</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">command_elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myCmd1</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabMyCmd1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommandElab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"ok\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hello</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ✓</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test1</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test2</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Broken: adding (docComment)? before the syntax category</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myCmd2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">docComment</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myKeyword</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">command_elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myCmd2</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabMyCmd2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommandElab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"ok2\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- some doc -/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hello</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ✓ (with docComment present)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hello</span><span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ✗ unexpected token 'foo'; expected command</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test2</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But converting the syntax category to a parser alias works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test3</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myKeyword2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"foo\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myCmd3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">docComment</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myKeyword2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">command_elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myCmd3</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabMyCmd3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommandElab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"ok3\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- some doc -/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hello</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ✓</span>\n<span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hello</span><span class=\"w\">                  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ✓</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Test3</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is the interaction between optional syntax (specifically <code>(docComment)?</code>) and <code>declare_syntax_cat</code> known to have limitations, or is this a bug?</p>\n<p>Any pointers would be appreciated, thanks!</p>",
